# deploy.sh runs on the server; it must be LF whoever commits it.
#
# The repo holds it as LF today only because this machine has
# core.autocrlf=true and normalises on the way in. A commit from a machine
# configured otherwise would carry CRLF into the repo, and bash answers a
# CRLF script with `$'\r': command not found` on the very first line —
# reproduced while testing the deploy pipeline in a Debian container.
*.sh text eol=lf
